{"$comment":"The root accepts one clone_inventory.json object, one clone_operations.jsonl logical record, one clone_postcheck.json object, or one prep_seal.json object. Inventory/postcheck are each capped at 8388608 canonical bytes, the final-LF hash-chained journal at 100000 records and 67108864 bytes, and the seal at 65536 bytes. Each journal record admits at most 32 simultaneous process observations and a distinct fail-closed batch of at most 32 completed wait records; this per-record wait batch is not a bound on total descendants across the 100000-record journal. Every observed byte/count/time/RSS/CPU/resource value is uint64 (uint63 only for monotonic clock samples) and is never clamped to the separately recorded admission ceilings. The process-overflow boolean equals live_process_count greater than the retained process array length; the wait count/overflow pair binds the actual batch count and retained first 32 records. Any overflow forces RESOURCE status and is forbidden on success. Canonical sorted-key compact UTF-8 JSON/JSONL, journal framing/hash/order, cross-file identity and storage-partition arithmetic, complete traversal, fsync, and Git predicates are external checks. clone_postcheck contains no terminal timer. prep_seal deliberately has no own identity/size or future Git field. The maximal witness is syntactic non-evidence.","$defs":{"absent_paths":{"items":false,"maxItems":18,"minItems":18,"prefixItems":[{"const":"script/__pycache__"},{"const":"script/a4_v2_archive.pyc"},{"const":"script/a4_v2_cache_policy_verifier.pyc"},{"const":"script/a4_v2_evidence.pyc"},{"const":"script/a4_v2_isolated_clone_prep.pyc"},{"const":"script/a4_v2_parity.pyc"},{"const":"script/a4_v2_producer.pyc"},{"const":"script/a4_v2_producer_wire.pyc"},{"const":"script/a4_v2_runner.pyc"},{"const":"script/a4_v2_verifier.pyc"},{"const":"script/run_arbitrary_cardinality_a4_v2.pyc"},{"const":"docs/saq_a4_v2_par_artifacts_2026_07_14.staging"},{"const":"docs/saq_a4_v2_par_artifacts_2026_